    "created_at": "2022-07-15T09:30:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-15T09:30:55Z",
    "body": "It wouldn't be to far fetched to think of a site which uses no-store explicitly to prevent bfcache. And it uses it so that loading a new page to the same tab won't keep the old page in bfcache. (Users don't explicitly logout)\r\n\r\nI'm just a tiny bit worried, since no-store has been the way to block bfcache since 2005.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
