    "created_at": "2025-05-20T09:51:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-20T09:54:28Z",
    "body": "\"Hidden as abuse\", seriously? 🤣\n\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html\n\n> This directive applies to both private and shared caches. \"MUST NOT store\" in this context means that the cache MUST NOT intentionally store the information in non-volatile storage and MUST make a best-effort attempt to remove the information from volatile storage as promptly as possible after forwarding it\n\nThis new behaviour very much doesn't sound like a \"best-effort attempt to remove the information from volatile storage as promptly as possible\", which I note is a `MUST` in the spec, not a `SHOULD`, `RECOMMENDED` or `MAY`.\n\nIf a dev has specified `Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate` their intent seems pretty clear, about as clear as your intent to intentionally ignore the spec and the dev's wishes!\n\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
